+# CA Soft Rules — leave a seed
+
+25 September 2026. The mature two-field comparison remains. A floor crossing brings its existing INJECT action into the visitor's route; it does not introduce a different solver or a new control panel.
+
+## Changes and decisions
+
+The map's existing rd_artifact gains seed:walk. Its wrapper passes this opt-in to ExchangeStudy, which mounts walk_seed.gd. A 1.5 × 1 m flush floor mark occupies the existing aisle at local (0,0,2.15). An Area3D receives the museum CharacterBody or XRToolsPlayerBody. This measures body-volume overlap, not pressure or mass. The first arrival writes the original nine-cell seed to both fields, once. Remaining inside does not replenish it; all visitors leaving rearms the mark. Props, hands and unrelated characters are ignored. No numerical time advances on entry. REPLAY while standing in the mark stays a clean held beginning until the next entrance.
+
+The existing eight controls, deterministic 32² solver, synchronous buffers, constants, wrapping, palettes and table/wall textures remain. COAT hides the walls while the floor mark remains available. The unconfigured exchange study has no receiver. All six artifacts, their roles, root placements, museum architecture and sequence order are retained. The already-present A/B discovery labels remain unnamed until the exchange intervention; no duplicate reveal mechanism was added.
+
+Only the manuscript's INJECT encounter is expanded, with one original native photograph. The preceding prose, three code excerpts, footnotes and entire clockmaker passage remain. Companion files explain the receiver and evidence; critical.md is unchanged.
+
+## What the experiment changed in our expectation
+
+The first behavioural run rejected an assumed outcome: the small seed did not persist more strongly at its centre with exchange. After the existing fields had run 100 updates, crossing wrote U=.5,V=.25 into x=3..5,y=14..16 in both. One further step gave the unseeded neighbour at (6,15) V=.02325669 in A, compared with .00332856 in a matched no-entry control; B remained zero there. Exchange carried some of the new concentration beyond the patch.
+
+After 100 further updates, its centre (4,15) held V=.00515910 in A and .03019554 in B. Both were below the planted .25. The image showed the small patch thinning while the earlier, larger pattern continued spreading. This is a result for this beginning, placement, timing and fixed parameter set, not a general law about all seeds. The rule and injection size were retained. The text now follows the observed dispersal rather than promising that connection guarantees survival.
+
+## Evidence and limits
+
+49 native assertions and eight actual museum mouse-ray events pass. Actual CharacterBody routes enter, leave, return and pass beside the mark. Entering changes exactly the existing nine U/V cells in both fields without a tick; staying does not reseed; REPLAY while occupied holds; a new entry writes once. Native tests cover unseeded witness arithmetic, boundary wrapping, scheduled +100, whole-image texture mapping, original controls, display/state separation, shared exchange equality, observation limit, duplicate configuration and the unconfigured study. Real XRTools class recognition is checked in code, not worn-headset behaviour.
+
+All recorded native artifact root placements match the before view. The final owned Godot process exits 0 with no GDScript errors; existing UID/environment/material/registry/generated-art warnings remain in the log. The fixture pauses automatic museum input/catch behaviour and supplies controlled body moves and local clock opportunities. No human headset, Quest performance, continuous gameplay, whole rear collection or learner acceptance is claimed.
+
+first-native/ retains the initial missing receiver caused by dynamic helper return type inference; explicit mesh types fixed it. seed-diagnostic/ retains the failed persistence expectation and its images. These failures precede the final passing run and are not hidden. Source hashes, exact text/source diffs and the final report accompany the review.
+
+No live museum plan, bake or save edits, frozen export refresh or commit. Shared core metadata changes only this hall, using a fresh read. Next: CA_AgentsCircuits, following the active sequence.
